          <p>Join the Community Foundation for a hands-on Grant Writing Workshop designed to help Teton Valley nonprofits strengthen their applications and increase their chances of securing funding.</p>

          <p>This workshop covers the fundamentals of compelling grant proposals — from crafting a clear narrative to building a realistic budget. Whether you're new to grant writing or looking to sharpen your skills, this session is for you.</p>

          <h2>What You'll Learn</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>How to align your project with funder priorities</li>
            <li>Writing a compelling needs statement</li>
            <li>Building budgets that tell a story</li>
            <li>Common mistakes and how to avoid them</li>
            <li>Tips specific to the CFTV Competitive Grant application</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Who Should Attend</h2>
          <p>This workshop is open to staff and board members of any 501(c)(3) nonprofit serving the Teton Valley region. No prior grant writing experience is required.</p>

          <p>Space is limited. Please register by April 5 to reserve your spot.</p>
